A||||8||Bill H||Need to lose lbs||||5||
Z||000000||Bill H||03-17-2001||10:00 PM||||Has anyone tried to put there fiero on a diet? I have an 88 formula and would like to get the weight down to 2400lbs. I will strip all of the a/c equip. lighter seats, lighter rims, where else can I save weight?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Black88GT||03-17-2001||10:10 PM||||Carpeting is pretty thick.  Make sure you remove all of the A/C parts.  There are shock absorbers under the front and rear bumpers you could remove.  Spare tire.  I think Held Motorsports sells tubular control arms and a tubular cradle, not cheap though but that would cut out a lot too.  All Radio equipment.  Thats all I can think of. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||skitime||03-17-2001||10:52 PM||||Glass weighs a lot too you could remove all but the windshield legally.||||reg||1
Z||000003||skitime||03-17-2001||11:00 PM||||How about the inner fender wells.  Useless weight. Heat shields, windshield washers. overflow bottle, smaller gas tank, power windows mirror and locks, spoiler, plastic supports under the bumpers, dash. Ok I know i am getting carried away.  Just go to a track and see what is left on a Fiero that is racing. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||ray b||03-17-2001||11:01 PM||||alloy block and heads ALCOA made the whole car alloy.remove all insulation, trim, headliner,center consold ect. heater core lines ducts blowers.<BR>trunk and front compartment could lose metal<BR>glass is heavy remove or replace with plastic.unnessary wires or lites, inner fenders liners  door guts, inner hood and rear cover plus springs and hinges and props for same. then cut, grind, and drill whats leftas much as you dare, but be safe not sorry. ray||||reg||1
Z||000005||EXHIBITER||03-18-2001||12:26 AM||||Huh?||||reg||1
Z||000006||LottaBallsCamaro||03-18-2001||12:28 AM||||You could remove all of those useless plastic body panels!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> When you replace glass its almost always lexan which will cost about 400 just for the windshield.<P>------------------<BR>91'RS 305TBI no mods to date<BR>92' Lumina 275,000 miles and still humping!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000007||GoCartGuy||03-18-2001||12:52 AM||||BTW, if you're replacing the glass, don't use normal Windex or the like on the Lexan.  Use either a vinegar water mixture, or get a cleaner specifically for platics.  Most aquarium stores carry cleaner for acrylic tanks, same stuff.  Normal glass cleaner with haze the surface permanently.<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT "The GoCart"||||reg||1
Z||000008||Old Lar||03-18-2001||10:14 AM||||Take out the seats, center console, dash and those useless guages, the interior door panels, and headliner.  Remove all the body panels drive with the space age frame.<P>If you do all ofthe above, you could knock off a half a ton of weight.||||reg||1
